WEBVTT

00:03.730 --> 00:04.710
Wow.

00:04.260 --> 00:06.230
Impressive as ever, Mr. Belgrieve.

00:05.360 --> 00:06.490
It's huge.

00:06.490 --> 00:10.120
Welp, butchering this thing won't be easy.

00:10.120 --> 00:13.790
It's incredible you took down 
that monster by yourself.

00:13.790 --> 00:16.020
More importantly, could you give me a hand?

00:16.020 --> 00:16.740
Sure thing.

00:18.110 --> 00:21.870
Thanks to you, we all feel 
safe working on the mountain.

00:21.870 --> 00:24.760
I'm not exactly doing it for the thanks.

00:25.760 --> 00:28.380
That's what we like about you.

00:28.380 --> 00:29.630
Don't make fun of me.

00:31.030 --> 00:33.880
Ange's spending another 
winter over there, huh?

00:38.120 --> 00:40.570
I hope I get to see her come spring.

00:53.400 --> 01:01.790
<b>My Daughter Left the Nest and Returned an S-Rank Adventurer</b>

02:12.520 --> 02:17.900
<b>Episode 3 "Welcome Home, Angeline"</b>

02:13.980 --> 02:15.220
This way!

02:15.220 --> 02:16.670
Hey, over here!

02:17.280 --> 02:18.500
It's been ages.

02:19.540 --> 02:21.580
I see a lot of people I don't recognize.

02:21.580 --> 02:22.990
You're right.

02:22.990 --> 02:25.730
But we sure know those guys over there.

02:26.970 --> 02:30.790
Lionel, you look like a mess.

02:30.790 --> 02:34.420
I can't believe things have gotten 
so dire you needed to call on us.

02:34.420 --> 02:37.580
General Muscles and Uncle Silver!

02:39.580 --> 02:41.420
If it isn't Ange!

02:43.660 --> 02:45.600
How've you been?

02:45.940 --> 02:49.230
Great! Who do you think I am?

02:50.090 --> 02:52.860
You haven't changed one bit.

02:53.250 --> 02:57.620
Come on, Cheborg. Don't slap her 
with all your muscleheaded might.

02:57.620 --> 03:00.230
Huh? You got something to say, Dortos?

03:00.230 --> 03:02.480
Don't shout in my ear, idiot.

03:02.480 --> 03:04.960
Huh?! What was that?!

03:05.750 --> 03:08.030
Who're the old dudes?

03:08.030 --> 03:11.130
They're retired S-rank adventurers.

03:11.130 --> 03:11.840
What?

03:12.650 --> 03:16.420
The guy in the military uniform 
is Cheborg the Annihilator.

03:16.420 --> 03:18.780
He's a former soldier of Estogal.

03:18.780 --> 03:23.210
The magical tattoos on his 
arms boost his strength.

03:23.210 --> 03:24.930
He can pulverize anything.

03:24.930 --> 03:27.980
The guy in white is the duchy's 
premier polearm master,

03:27.980 --> 03:29.500
Dortos the Silver.

03:29.500 --> 03:34.390
Two grown men together
could barely lift his weapon,

03:34.390 --> 03:36.700
but he wields it with one hand.

03:36.700 --> 03:39.670
In other words, they're both monsters...

03:39.670 --> 03:42.930
If you're here, does that mean 
you've resumed adventuring?

03:42.930 --> 03:47.140
Yes. With so many monsters about,
 we had no choice.

03:47.140 --> 03:51.490
That's right. The young guns
are a bunch of weaklings.

03:51.490 --> 03:55.520
All right! I'm so glad you both came back!

03:56.270 --> 03:59.700
Well done, Guild Master! Thank you.

04:01.370 --> 04:04.380
Only because you kept begging me to do it.

04:04.380 --> 04:06.760
It wasn't cheap, though.

04:07.260 --> 04:09.530
I don't know how I'll live from now on...

04:10.860 --> 04:15.890
We haven't seen monsters like this
for the past century.

04:15.890 --> 04:18.400
Still, it took you long enough to act on it.

04:20.070 --> 04:23.150
I know, I know. I'm incompetent.

04:23.150 --> 04:26.560
By the way, why'd you 
gather this many people?

04:27.170 --> 04:29.240
Now that we've got enough hands,

04:29.240 --> 04:31.960
we can take down the cause 
of this monster outbreak.

04:36.290 --> 04:39.280
You... know what's causing it?

04:39.280 --> 04:43.260
I only put it together yesterday, 
so I don't have proof...

04:43.260 --> 04:45.410
but I think a Demon King has returned.

04:46.030 --> 04:48.470
A Demon King? Truly?

04:48.470 --> 04:52.840
I can't say for sure. There's a limit
to what I can investigate myself.

04:53.280 --> 04:56.670
I'm having someone else confirm 
my suspicions right now.

04:56.670 --> 04:58.280
You were looking into it alone?

04:58.530 --> 05:00.390
My employees are regular citizens,

05:00.390 --> 05:03.360
so the most I can have them do 
is search through documents.

05:03.360 --> 05:06.060
You could've gone to low-ranking adventurers.

05:06.060 --> 05:09.340
No way. I can't send low-rankers out

05:09.340 --> 05:12.180
where high-rank monsters are appearing.

05:12.180 --> 05:14.530
I'm a former S-rank, you know.

05:14.530 --> 05:18.130
Then you could've asked high-rankers 
to help in their spare time.

05:19.840 --> 05:24.150
It takes more than a day or two 
to conduct an investigation.

05:24.150 --> 05:26.310
People would get furious and walk out

05:26.310 --> 05:28.800
if I asked them to help
when they're already so busy.

05:28.800 --> 05:34.300
So in the end, I had to fight a bunch
of powerful monsters by myself.

05:36.790 --> 05:39.860
I had no idea. I can't believe I lectured you

05:39.860 --> 05:42.640
when you've been working so hard on your own.

05:42.640 --> 05:43.850
I'm sorry.

05:44.170 --> 05:48.310
No, it's fine! You're actually 
the only one who got angry at me.

05:48.310 --> 05:49.100
What?

05:49.100 --> 05:52.980
If people don't like what's going on,
they normally just leave without a word.

05:52.980 --> 05:56.130
But you gave me an earful.

05:56.130 --> 05:59.450
It was the push I needed. Thank you.

06:02.400 --> 06:07.330
It's not boring adults, but children who 
charge ahead that make the world go round.

06:07.330 --> 06:11.070
We wouldn't be here if you hadn't 
begged him to reach out to us.

06:11.070 --> 06:14.720
That's right. So don't worry about it, Ange.

06:15.760 --> 06:16.720
Okay.

06:23.430 --> 06:24.570
Someone's there.

06:25.360 --> 06:28.360
Maria, anything unusual to report?

06:28.870 --> 06:34.360
No, but there's definitely a 
warped mass of magic out there.

06:34.640 --> 06:39.130
Not only that, but someone's erected a 
barrier around it in order to hide it.

06:39.130 --> 06:40.740
Whoever did it is pretty skilled.

06:40.740 --> 06:41.720
What?

06:41.720 --> 06:43.390
Is this the place?

06:43.390 --> 06:45.870
I thought this was an E-rank dungeon.

06:45.870 --> 06:49.270
We must not have noticed 
because of the barrier.

06:51.120 --> 06:57.030
How could you abandon a poor girl all 
alone in a place as dangerous as this?

06:57.030 --> 07:01.180
Don't get me wrong.
I sent you <i>because</i> it's dangerous.

07:01.180 --> 07:02.510
Granny Maria!

07:03.310 --> 07:05.470
Well, if it isn't Ange.

07:05.470 --> 07:08.000
I'm still a spring chicken.
Don't call me "granny."

07:08.560 --> 07:10.770
How are you a spring chicken?

07:10.770 --> 07:13.660
You're an old hag and you know it.

07:13.660 --> 07:16.790
Who are you calling a hag,
 you dumbass apprentice?!

07:16.790 --> 07:19.540
I'm still a spry 68 years old!

07:19.540 --> 07:23.660
You can stop your aging with magic, 
but being 68 still makes you old!

07:22.460 --> 07:25.280
Shut up! How dare you speak 
that way to your master?!

07:26.670 --> 07:29.530
I see your cough hasn't gotten any better.

07:29.530 --> 07:31.540
You still haven't developed a cure?

07:31.540 --> 07:36.420
Nah, not yet. Dragons' curses are nasty.

07:38.930 --> 07:41.820
Did you hear that? 
She said it's a dragon's curse.

07:41.820 --> 07:43.450
Does that mean she's...

07:43.450 --> 07:47.680
Yeah. That's former S-rank adventurer 
Maria the Dragonslayer.

07:48.390 --> 07:52.030
She came into contact with cursed
 blood felling an S-rank dragon.

07:52.030 --> 07:54.020
She hasn't stopped coughing since.

07:54.300 --> 07:56.590
So he called you in too, huh?

07:56.590 --> 07:57.940
Sure enough.

07:57.940 --> 08:01.750
I swear... What'd he gather 
all the old farts for?

08:01.750 --> 08:03.710
You haven't changed one bit.

08:03.710 --> 08:05.760
Still faking that illness?

08:05.760 --> 08:09.840
I told you, it's not fake, you meathead!

08:09.840 --> 08:12.960
Um... If you don't mind,
 I'd like to continue.

08:14.430 --> 08:22.260
I think we can stop this monster outbreak 
by destroying the mass of magic in there.

08:22.530 --> 08:24.120
Do you have a plan?

08:26.020 --> 08:28.360
This many powerful warriors 
should be enough.

08:29.580 --> 08:32.240
Okay, that's enough talk.

08:32.240 --> 08:35.920
We just need to destroy the damn thing!

08:39.960 --> 08:42.230
Wait, wh-what are you...

08:48.040 --> 08:49.840
What?!

08:53.070 --> 08:55.870
Well, the barrier's gone.

09:05.770 --> 09:08.110
What have you done?!

09:09.520 --> 09:12.170
What's the problem? This makes things simple.

09:12.590 --> 09:13.850
Hey, Demon King!

09:13.850 --> 09:15.670
Come on out!

09:16.260 --> 09:18.210
I won't let you steal a march on me.

09:18.210 --> 09:20.860
Oh, yeah? Suit yourself!

09:22.160 --> 09:25.610
Give me a break... 
The seniors have started without us.

09:25.610 --> 09:30.040
Let's at least make things 
as easy as possible for them.

09:30.040 --> 09:31.730
Yeah!

09:44.040 --> 09:45.380
What is that?

09:45.380 --> 09:47.040
Gross!

09:47.040 --> 09:52.120
Looks like the warped magic 
caused some monsters to merge.

09:53.370 --> 09:55.110
Follow my lead, dunce.

09:55.420 --> 09:57.110
Who do you think you are?

09:57.510 --> 10:01.120
Ecliptic in the heavens, 
path of particles of light...

10:01.560 --> 10:04.680
A single particle makes waves,

10:04.680 --> 10:07.820
falling to form a shimmering 
mirage on the ground.

10:08.590 --> 10:09.910
Imperial Thunder!

10:17.090 --> 10:19.390
Nice assist, Anessa.

10:20.150 --> 10:21.140
Thank you.

10:24.970 --> 10:26.930
We'll be at a disadvantage if this drags on.

10:26.930 --> 10:30.060
We need to defeat whatever's inside there.

10:30.060 --> 10:33.210
Uncle Silver, we're not getting 
anywhere like this.

10:33.820 --> 10:36.110
Leave the small fry to the others
 while we charge!

10:37.130 --> 10:39.600
Makes sense to me. Cheborg, let's go.

10:39.900 --> 10:42.120
Huh? Did you say something?

10:48.530 --> 10:50.470
What is this?

10:54.450 --> 10:57.640
This place looks rather different.

10:57.640 --> 10:59.120
Where's the heart of the dungeon?

10:59.120 --> 11:01.540
There are so many monsters, 
I can't sense it.

11:05.540 --> 11:06.340
Ange!

11:11.000 --> 11:12.960
Don't let your guard down.

11:12.960 --> 11:15.010
Thanks, General Muscles!

11:15.010 --> 11:15.820
Huh?

11:21.320 --> 11:24.380
This one seems a bit tough.

11:24.380 --> 11:26.850
I was hoping to land the 
first blow on the Demon King,

11:26.850 --> 11:28.400
but let me handle this one!

11:29.120 --> 11:32.520
Whatever you want. Let's go, Ange.

11:32.520 --> 11:34.630
Be careful, General Muscles.

11:34.630 --> 11:37.530
Sure. I'll just be here having fun.

11:50.260 --> 11:51.710
Which way?

11:51.710 --> 11:54.870
<i>This won't do. Dad would laugh at me.</i>

11:55.310 --> 12:01.880
<i>Think back... He said a boss monster's 
presence feels like it pricks your skin.</i>

12:05.620 --> 12:06.750
This way!

12:06.750 --> 12:07.620
Got it.

12:12.120 --> 12:16.670
<i>There's no mistaking it. The prickling 
sensation is getting stronger.</i>

12:17.400 --> 12:22.690
<i>I've fought countless S-rank monsters, 
but I've never felt anything like this.</i>

12:32.970 --> 12:36.080
This seems to be the heart of the dungeon.

12:36.080 --> 12:36.720
Yeah.

12:39.420 --> 12:42.360
Master, I'm so lonely.

12:42.360 --> 12:43.710
Where are you?

12:44.210 --> 12:46.440
That's the Demon King?

12:46.930 --> 12:50.700
Ange, don't let your guard down. 
Something seems off here.

12:53.920 --> 12:57.340
<i>This is definitely the
 heart of the warped magic.</i>

12:57.340 --> 13:00.220
<i>But it's unnerving how 
little hostility I detect.</i>

13:02.190 --> 13:05.720
Where did you go, Master?

13:07.780 --> 13:10.340
Why are you so sad?

13:11.020 --> 13:12.910
Who's your master?

13:15.200 --> 13:16.100
Ange!

13:16.490 --> 13:19.080
Can I see you if I kill more?

13:26.730 --> 13:28.250
I can't pierce it.

13:28.250 --> 13:31.410
Guess they don't call it a
 Demon King for nothing.

13:32.230 --> 13:35.500
I'm so lonely, Master.

13:36.250 --> 13:38.180
I'm sorry. I let my guard down.

13:38.180 --> 13:39.760
It's okay. Look alive.

13:44.510 --> 13:45.510
<i>I can't cut it?</i>

13:45.510 --> 13:47.390
Take this!

13:59.140 --> 14:00.870
Uncle, are you all right?

14:00.870 --> 14:02.200
I'm sorry, Ange.

14:02.200 --> 14:05.780
I can't believe it cracked 
my magic-coated polearm.

14:06.020 --> 14:08.770
I'll take point. Can you back me up?

14:08.770 --> 14:10.660
Yes. I'm ashamed I can't do more.

14:25.000 --> 14:27.310
<i>I still can't properly cut through it.</i>

14:28.150 --> 14:32.180
It's like a mass of 
high-density magic, but...

14:32.910 --> 14:36.180
My body moves before I think.

14:36.630 --> 14:40.390
<i>When's the last time I felt 
like my life was in danger?</i>

14:40.390 --> 14:41.620
I miss you.

14:42.420 --> 14:44.780
Master, where are you?

14:44.780 --> 14:46.690
Ba'al is here...

14:47.300 --> 14:48.770
I miss you.

14:50.160 --> 14:52.700
I don't know who it is 
that you want to see...

14:53.690 --> 14:56.700
<i>But there's someone I want to see, too!</i>

14:57.360 --> 15:01.200
<i>That's right... This thing is 
the reason I can't go home.</i>

15:01.200 --> 15:03.100
If you want to see them so badly...

15:12.790 --> 15:15.300
Go see them already!

15:20.340 --> 15:22.270
Master...

15:30.030 --> 15:33.320
Uncle, what happened to it?

15:36.640 --> 15:39.210
You won, Ange.

15:50.540 --> 15:52.280
Where am I?

15:52.910 --> 15:54.770
A room at the guild infirmary.

15:55.960 --> 16:00.100
Ange, I'm so glad you're okay!

16:00.100 --> 16:04.100
Miri, calm down! You're hurting my shoulder!

16:04.100 --> 16:06.660
Come on, get off of her.

16:07.530 --> 16:08.360
Ow...

16:09.920 --> 16:11.780
I'm glad you're all right.

16:11.780 --> 16:14.160
I can't believe you took out a Demon King.

16:15.200 --> 16:16.670
How are the others?

16:16.670 --> 16:18.620
They're all fine.

16:18.620 --> 16:21.540
Maria said her throat hurt
and went home, though.

16:21.540 --> 16:24.050
Talk about a heartless old bag.

16:25.440 --> 16:27.550
Good... I'm glad.

16:29.740 --> 16:31.140
Ms. Angeline!

16:31.560 --> 16:32.800
Ms. Angeline!

16:31.800 --> 16:34.220
Our hero, the Demon King killer!

16:32.800 --> 16:34.090
Thank you!

16:34.220 --> 16:36.050
Protector of Orphen!

16:36.460 --> 16:38.480
Stop. You're embarrassing me.

16:38.480 --> 16:41.270
Ange, you're a hero.

16:41.270 --> 16:42.620
That hurts.

16:42.620 --> 16:44.320
Ah, s-sorry.

16:44.700 --> 16:47.450
Ms. Ange, thank you so much.

16:47.450 --> 16:51.030
All that's left is to clean up the
 remaining monsters posing a threat.

16:51.260 --> 16:54.020
So there's still more work to do?

16:54.370 --> 16:57.040
No, actually... Well?

16:57.040 --> 16:59.940
We'll handle them.

16:59.940 --> 17:02.540
Take all the time off that you want.

17:03.490 --> 17:06.490
Then you'll keep adventuring for a while?

17:07.800 --> 17:10.060
Come to think of it, I'm starved.

17:10.060 --> 17:11.950
Should we go to our regular place, then?

17:11.950 --> 17:15.660
Let's go! You must be feeling 
better if you're hungry.

17:15.660 --> 17:17.670
By the way, Ange...

17:18.540 --> 17:23.000
Lionel told me what happened. 
I'm impressed you didn't run off.

17:23.000 --> 17:27.320
A typical adventurer would've gotten 
sick of this and fled to another guild.

17:27.320 --> 17:30.390
Defeating monsters day in and day out...

17:30.390 --> 17:34.310
Worse yet, you've been wanting
 to see your father, haven't you?

17:34.750 --> 17:39.610
If I left, it wouldn't be the guild
 that suffered. It would be the people.

17:41.990 --> 17:43.610
Ms. Ange...

17:43.610 --> 17:48.140
At first, I was angry. 
I kept wondering, "Why me?"

17:48.530 --> 17:53.260
But my dad said strong adventurers
help the weak.

17:53.860 --> 17:58.150
He wouldn't like it if 
I abandoned Orphen to come home.

18:02.360 --> 18:04.640
You've got a good dad.

18:04.640 --> 18:05.890
I agree.

18:05.890 --> 18:10.390
Good grief. You've made me realize 
just how small a man I am.

18:12.140 --> 18:17.360
So your father was the reason 
you remained at the guild?

18:17.360 --> 18:20.650
Sounds like I owe him an awful lot.

18:20.980 --> 18:24.160
That's right. My dad is an incredible man.

18:24.520 --> 18:27.890
They call him Belgrieve the Red Ogre!

18:32.820 --> 18:36.060
I underestimated Orphen's guild.

18:36.060 --> 18:37.830
I presumed incompetence.

18:37.830 --> 18:39.180
I didn't think they'd find this.

18:49.150 --> 18:53.080
But the biggest threat is 
that Black-Haired Valkyrie.

18:53.790 --> 18:58.250
No matter. I'm only just getting started.

19:06.700 --> 19:09.210
Man, the air here is delicious!

19:10.410 --> 19:13.740
Right? The air in these parts is so clean.

19:13.740 --> 19:17.970
I bet it'd be great for the old hag's lungs.

19:17.970 --> 19:20.230
Miri, you must really love Granny Maria.

19:20.840 --> 19:24.610
N-Nuh-uh. I don't give two toots about her.

19:25.480 --> 19:27.850
If you say so.

19:34.700 --> 19:38.960
Nothing has changed 
since I left here five years ago.

19:40.270 --> 19:42.830
<i>My hair has grown longer, 
and I've grown taller.</i>

19:43.400 --> 19:45.360
<i>But I still feel exactly the same.</i>

19:46.080 --> 19:47.750
<i>What about Dad?</i>

19:48.270 --> 19:53.880
<i>I've missed him more than anything,
but how does he feel?</i>

19:54.880 --> 19:58.820
<i>He looks after the children of Turnera.</i>

19:59.390 --> 20:02.120
<i>I'm sure he cares for them 
like they're his own.</i>

20:03.010 --> 20:07.980
<i>I heard Countess Bordeaux approached him,
 but he turned her down.</i>

20:09.190 --> 20:12.810
<i>What if he rejected 
her advances because of me?</i>

20:13.280 --> 20:16.530
<i>What if I'm holding him back 
from what he wants to do?</i>

20:17.470 --> 20:21.100
<i>What if he's just fine without me?</i>

20:21.570 --> 20:25.650
<i>What if he's not that excited 
to see me again?</i>

20:26.540 --> 20:30.300
<i>What if he secretly doesn't 
care about me anymore?</i>

20:33.700 --> 20:35.970
<i>My dad isn't like that.</i>

20:35.970 --> 20:37.100
Ange!

20:37.550 --> 20:39.810
Which way should we go from here?

21:06.750 --> 21:10.340
You know, I worked really, really hard!

21:10.650 --> 21:13.750
I reached rank S and beat 
a bunch of monsters!

21:13.750 --> 21:16.400
I helped people in need, too!

21:16.400 --> 21:18.980
The other day, I beat a Demon King!

21:18.980 --> 21:21.840
Um, I... I...

21:24.590 --> 21:26.730
I, um...

21:27.840 --> 21:29.790
You've grown so much.

21:33.200 --> 21:35.020
Your hair's gotten long.

21:35.020 --> 21:36.530
It looks good on you.

21:39.070 --> 21:39.950
Thanks.

21:40.450 --> 21:44.760
You've grown into such a fine woman, 
I didn't recognize you at first.

21:53.880 --> 21:56.240
Welcome home, Ange.

21:57.370 --> 21:59.700
It's good to be back, Dad!

23:35.010 --> 23:39.970
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.010 --> 23:39.970
<b>"Quiet Days in Turnera with the Occasional Family Spat"</b>
